Package: bicountbrms
Title: Joint Bivariate-Count brms Custom Families for Paired Counts
Version: 0.9.1
Date: 2026-08-06
Authors@R:
    person("Adam N. H.", "Smith", , "anhsmith@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0059-6206"))
Description: Provides custom brms families for comparing two paired count
    sources, modelling the pair jointly via trivariate reduction rather than
    reducing it to a difference. Four families are supplied: a bivariate
    Poisson (bipois), its overdispersed bivariate Negative-Binomial sibling
    (binegbin), and a censoring-aware extension of each (bipois_cens,
    binegbin_cens) that admits rows on which one of the two counts is
    unobserved, through the integrated-out marginal of the same joint model.
    Modelling the pair rather than its difference captures the overall level,
    the correlation between sources, and marginal overdispersion alongside the
    disagreement, and supports simulating one count conditional on the other,
    including on rows where it was never recorded. An interpretable
    reparameterisation separates overall level, congruence, and source bias,
    giving each a finite null and so admitting penalised-complexity priors.
    The Negative-Binomial families let the two source-specific components
    differ in overdispersion.
